  "description": "Minnesota's 2nd Congressional District is an open seat in 2026 after six-term incumbent Democrat Angie Craig chose to run for the U.S. Senate instead of seeking re-election. The district covers the southern Twin Cities suburbs including Burnsville, Eagan, Lakeville, and extends into rural areas of Dakota, Scott, and Le Sueur counties. With a Cook Partisan Voting Index of D+3, it is the most evenly divided congressional district in Minnesota and one of the most competitive open House seats in the country. The Democratic primary features three well-known state legislators plus two additional candidates, while state Senator Eric Pratt is the presumptive Republican nominee, setting up a high-stakes general election contest for control of a key swing seat.",
